 "notes": "Curve traced from vector paths of Fig. 3 (e-print file Fig2.pdf): the solid blue 'Energy deposition' contour for the low-energy-supernova case (Rprog=5e13 cm, Edep=0.1 B=1e50 erg), the paper's tightest bound ('even tighter bounds obtained from low-energy SNe observations'). The excluded region is a closed island: points trace the lower boundary from 1 MeV up in mass, around the high-mass tip (~556 MeV), then back along the upper (trapping-regime ceiling) boundary, so mass is not monotonic. Alternative scenario in the same figure: normal CCSN bound (Rprog=3e12 cm, Edep=1 B), thick blue contour, roughly a factor ~3 weaker on the floor and lower ceiling. Astrophysical energy-deposition argument (SFHo-18.8 muonic PNS model); no formal statistical confidence level is quoted, 0.95 entered as placeholder. No dark-matter density assumption. Contour clipped to the displayed window m_a in [1,1000] MeV, g in [1e-11,1e-4] GeV^-1; masses converted MeV -> eV.",
